A||||5||js||Squeeking polyeurethane bushings||||1||
Z||000000||js||12-19-1999||10:06 PM||||Any of you experience squeeking polyeurethane bushings? Mine have definitely begun to squeek with the cold temperatures now ( below about 32F ). I used plenty of the Prothane grease. Any suggestions?<P>Thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||superXmotorsports||12-20-1999||12:04 AM||||In my experience they always squeak.  Especially when cold.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000002||dogtired||12-20-1999||03:19 AM||||Not me but my brother had a Ford with that type of bushing. What he did was use a spray lubricant on them. Now the strange part,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and my brother is strange  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> He would get the cheepest he could find, because the top of the line brands would evaporite faster. The cheeper had more oil content and would last longer? His method was to spray the bushings everytime he checked his oil. Thats all I know! Hope it helps.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||01:39 PM||||This is gonna sound odd (well...normal coming from me) and it might be a little late for you, but try using some 5th wheel grease for a truck.  I had the same problem with the poly stops for the hood on an International and the only thing that would keep them from squeaking was the 5th wheel grease.  It's cheap and you can find it at any truckstop in the world.  If you don't understand what I'm talking about, email me and I'll explain.  BTW-the stuff lasts forever.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||12-23-1999||02:27 PM||||I'd say it's normal.  Put some on my 914 and it began squeaking after a month.  Used lots of the grease that came with the bushing.  I've always heard from eveyone that they squeak.  It is a much harder bushing than the spongy rubber.  I wouldn't worry too much.  "It wasn't built for comfort, it was built for speed" - Jim Steinman.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tim||12-23-1999||03:53 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/tips.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/tips.htm</A> <BR>Read #1.  The rest is good also.||||reg||1
